A||||10||lowfunds||Quarter window assembly removal?????||||1||
Z||000000||lowfunds||01-10-2001||06:04 PM||||Does anyone know how to remove the assembly without breaking the holding tabs? I need to remove them because I have another car with good windows that I can just swap over. Thanks for any info.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-10-2001||06:24 PM||||There is a bolt that has to be removed on the inside. It can be accessed from under the panel with the seat belt on it. I will take pics of the ones on my parts car and post them tomorrow.||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowfunds||01-10-2001||06:41 PM||||Thank you I will look for the pics. I did not see the info in my chilton, but then again it seems like all the info I NEED is never in there. Thank God for all you guys, you have proven to be very helpful. Thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||01-10-2001||06:52 PM||||Depending on the nut used, it will be either a 10 or 11mm. You will need to remove the top seatbelt bolt (T-45 Torx?), the side trim(Philips) and remove the interiro panel. Then you can access the quarter panel nut through the hole. If it drops, you should be able to retreive it through the vent at the bottom. <P>Depending on the clips use, you will need a long thin screwdriver or blade to release the clips on the diagonal side.<P>TK ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||01-10-2001||07:42 PM||||See Paul McKibben's "How To" section at<BR>- <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||01-10-2001||10:14 PM||||The bolt is only on the 84's.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||01-10-2001||10:47 PM||||There is a stud on all models, not just the '84. On the '84 this MUST be removed but not necessary on the following models. There is another method that I believe you will find in the directed link, but I think that removing the nut is easier!||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowfunds||01-11-2001||06:37 PM||||Thanks... also have any of you replaced the rivets on the rocker panels? What did you use? Is the fiero store and salvage yards the only place to find fasteners, or can other fastners be used in there place? sorry for all the questions, Just been to busy to shop around at parts departments to find out what all can be made to fit,if fastners are broken or do not hold correctly anymore. Because I see most of them are no longer made. Thanks again||||reg||1
