Z||000009||lowfunds||01-11-2001||08:25 PM||||You did not let me down, the info itself is enough. The fact you would go to the trouble of posting picts is above and beyond. I am doing a complete teardown of my 87gt and want to be as cautious as possible, as not to break anything that can not be replaced easily. I am also swapping parts from a 86 coupe to an 85se. So anything I pick up from others that have done this is great. Again anyone on the forum who gives correct advice is not a let down to anyone. Thank you all for the info. While Im thinking about it does anyone know of a good site that details the teardown and assembly of a car? Thanks again||||reg||1
Z||000010||MrPBody||01-11-2001||08:35 PM||||<I>re</I>: rocker panel rivets --<P>I through-bolted the lower edge with black nylon license plate fasteners and a dab of blue Loctite.  In the door sill, I used Rivet-tite (Motormite) black screw rivets . . . I forget the part number.  You can get the rivets from GM, but they're pricey and you need a 1/4" rivet gun.<BR>||||reg||1
